# The Forts | INT/EXT | Wheelhouse, Passing The Inner Batteries | NIGHT | abram, jolly | Go slowly | The captain's lazy speed. Arms folded on the sill as he folds them. The whistle: two long, one short. A lantern swings: pass | | 7 | water, vehicles=side-wheel steamer, vfx=harbour forts at night
# The Forts | INT | Hold | NIGHT | hester, jolly | Keep them quiet | Children on sacks. The engine's beat, held down. {jolly} shows her where the powder is, in case. She says he will not need it | | 5 | crowd=10, props=powder keg
# The Forts | INT/EXT | Wheelhouse, Under The Last Fort | DAWN | abram, the_sentry | Be seen | First light. A face could be read now. Two long, one short. Nothing. Then a shout from the wall to give them hell. He lifts one hand, as the captain does | The last fort is passed | 8 | water, vehicles=side-wheel steamer, vfx=sea fort at dawn
# The Fleet | EXT | Harbour Bar | DAWN | abram, jolly | Not turn | Out of range, she should swing along the coast. She steers straight out. Behind, a signal gun, too late | The fort understands | 5 | water, vehicles=side-wheel steamer, vfx=cannon fire falling short
# The Fleet | EXT | Open Water, Fog | DAWN | abram, hester, jolly | Be believed | A warship's ports open. A gunner with a lanyard. {hester}'s bedsheet goes up the staff, grey in the mist. The sun reaches it. He takes off the hat | They are free | 7 | water, vehicles=side-wheel steamer+blockade warship, vfx=fog and sunrise, props=bedsheet
